# relay-service-users.env — shared EnvironmentFile for the relay-ro / relay-svc hardened
# systemd --user units (id:5bef, authoring half of id:8e7a).
#
# WHY LITERAL PATHS, NOT %h (Amendment-2 F3, Fable review — binding, do not rediscover):
# under relay-ro's / relay-svc's OWN --user manager, %h resolves to /home/relay-ro or
# /home/relay-svc respectively — NEVER /home/tobias. Every default the two entrypoint
# scripts fall back to is a `${VAR:-$HOME/...}` expansion baked for the LOGIN user's home,
# so under the service users' own managers those defaults would silently point at
# .config/relay trees the service users just created and own themselves — never the tree
# apply-relay-acls.sh (id:02c7) actually applied the write matrix to. Every $HOME-relative
# override each script reads is spelled out below as a literal /home/tobias/... path, so
# both hardened units see the SAME ~/.config/relay tree tobias's own (unsandboxed)
# dogfood units use — reachability is then scoped down only by the POSIX ACLs already in
# place plus this file's ReadOnlyPaths/ReadWritePaths carve-outs, never by a differing
# default.
#
# Loaded via EnvironmentFile= in relay-ro-discover-repos-mechanical.service and
# relay-svc-mechanical-daemon.service (this directory). RELAY_REQUIRE_SERVICE_USER is set
# per-unit via Environment= instead (its value differs by user), not here.
#
# id:8e7a's run half installs this file read-only under /etc/systemd/user/ alongside the
# unit files it references — id:5bef only authors the text; it is never sourced/executed,
# only parsed by systemd's EnvironmentFile= loader (KEY=VALUE lines, no quoting/expansion).

# --- discover-repos-mechanical.sh (relay-ro, id:9d97) ---
RELAY_TOML=/home/tobias/.config/relay/relay.toml
SRC_DIR=/home/tobias/src
RELAY_DISCOVERY_QUEUE_DIR=/home/tobias/.config/relay/discovery-queue
RELAY_WORKTREE_BASE=/home/tobias/.cache/relay/worktrees
RELAY_DISCOVER_MECH_LOG=/home/tobias/.claude/logs/discover-repos-mechanical.log
HEARTBEAT_BASE=/home/tobias/.config/relay/heartbeats

# --- mechanical-daemon.sh (relay-svc, id:b3d0) ---
RELAY_RECIPE_DIR=/home/tobias/.config/relay/recipes
RELAY_INTENSITY_FILE=/home/tobias/.config/relay/permitted-intensity.json
CLAIM_BASE=/home/tobias/.config/relay
CLAIM_LOG=/home/tobias/.claude/logs/relay-claim.log
INJECT_BASE=/home/tobias/.config/relay
INJECT_LOG=/home/tobias/.claude/logs/relay-inject.log
MECHANICAL_DAEMON_LOG=/home/tobias/.claude/logs/mechanical-daemon.log
